  "scope": "CPU-only opt-in parallel giant-group ranges for retained RNS S2C. --s2c-group-workers N limits the outer team; default0 keeps the original serial coordinator.",
  "algorithm": "Sort groups by descending giant index for Horner mode, split the ordered groups into contiguous ranges, and evaluate each range with unchanged per-group exact convolution, CRT reconstruction and rounding. Each range performs its own Horner recurrence and final absolute rotation to the common output frame; merge range ciphertexts in fixed order modulo the output modulus. Non-Horner mode preserves each independent group rotation. Horner range boundaries change key-switch decomposition/noise, so full outputs require fresh independent accuracy qualification.",
  "concurrency": "Requires a retained prepared output-cache readiness hook before workers start. Input baby spectra and public group spectra are immutable. Each worker owns matrix sums, CRT and ciphertext temporaries; FFT processor scratch is thread-local. Nested OpenMP teams are locally suppressed, caller policy restored, and worker exceptions propagate after the team joins.",
  "worker_and_memory_bound": "Team size=min(requested cap, group count, OpenMP maximum), falling back to serial inside an existing parallel team. Partial ciphertexts, matrix/CRT and key-switch temporaries grow with this bounded team. No extra prepared key spectra; FFT thread-local workspace can persist with runtime threads. CLI caps requests at64.",
  "timing_counter_semantics": "s2c_seconds is end-to-end wall time. s2c_group_worker_wall_seconds measures parallel range evaluation plus merge. With parallel ranges, matrix/inverse_crt/giant_rotations fields sum worker durations and overlap; they must not be interpreted as separate wall-time stages. Report explicitly marks worker-sum semantics. Rotation call/bit counters still count total work.",
